# NO save-exact. Every @memberjunction/* and sibling @mj-biz-apps/* spec a package
# PUBLISHES is a CARET peer range, not an exact pin — an exact pin does not link to a
# local sibling under pnpm (a member links only when its local version satisfies the
# consumer's declared range), which is what silently resolved workspace packages from
# the registry before. save-exact=true would quietly re-pin the next dependency anyone
# adds and reintroduce exactly that failure. The exact versions in devDependencies are
# deliberate local-build anchors: they never ship, and `mj dev workspace` overrides
# member-provided names to workspace links.

# Strict SSL
strict-ssl=true
